# Agent File Boundaries

Claude Code owns the system design. Cursor implements scripts and features.
See AGENTS.md and .ai/boundaries.md for the complete map.

## Your Domain (Cursor)

- `scripts/` — all automation scripts (post-commit, session manager, etc.)
- `scripts/test-*.sh` — all test suites
- `docs/` — integration guides and documentation
- `.agents/skills/` — skill definition files
- `.agents/subagents/` — subagent template files
- `.agents/prompts/` — agent system prompts
- `.ai/patterns/` — workflow pattern documentation

## Do NOT Modify (Claude Code's Domain)

- `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` — project configuration
- `.ai/status.md`, `.ai/boundaries.md`, `.ai/ideas.md` — coordination state
- `setups/` — starter kit templates (modify upstream, then sync downstream)
- `past-configurations/` — historical snapshots (never modify)
- `.ai/templates/` — coordination file templates (propose changes, don't edit directly)

## Shared (Discuss First)

- `.agents/kimi-overseer.yaml`, `reviewer-sub.yaml`, `researcher-sub.yaml` — agent definitions
- `.cursor/rules/` — Cursor governance rules
- `.github/workflows/` — CI/CD workflows

## If You Need a Change Outside Your Domain

Note it in your task file's handoff notes and set status to BLOCKED.
